<SCENARIO VER="105">
{PLAYSND "システム音\The_Lampe.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{CREATECG "立木三日" "グラフィック\立ち絵\人物\イラスト\立木三日2.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "300" "" "0" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{CREATECG "プレート" "グラフィック\システム\立木三日プレート.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "180" "380" "600" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{CHANGECG "立木三日" "グラフィック\立ち絵\人物\イラスト\立木三日.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
<TXSPN>Thank you for your hard work, <VAR NAME="プレイヤー名" unk3="50">-sama. With this, the Meicho Arc [Clear Sign] and the Wabigoto Arc [Apology] are entirely finished―<PG>
Or so I thought, but judging by your progress through the Wabigoto Arc [Apology], it seems you missed collecting one.<PG>
Well, there is no need to concern yourself with it now. I will guide you as appropriate.<PG>
Now, it was an ending with a truly bad aftertaste, but this is the truth of the Motoki-cho flaying case. Murdered by Mifuyu Niimura, who was trying to protect Haruka Niimura.<PG>
The Niimura family and the Kogori family fought over one daughter, and as a result it led to endings that were ghastly, each and every one, like the ones you saw in the endings of the Jusatsu Arc [Killing by Curse].<PG>
However, if only the Megasawa City case had never happened in the first place, such tragedies should have been avoided, and a new future should have opened up.<PG>
Yes, that route in which the Niimura family and the Kogori family truly reconciled still has a continuation.<PG>
Natsumi Kogori, who went to the Arata settlement for Eiichiro Niimura's thirteenth-year memorial service, and the Kogori couple seeing her off with worried looks. [TN: Buddhist memorials count the year of death as the first year.]<PG>
Who would have predicted that this would be the curtain-raiser of a new tragedy?
{PAUSE ""}
{}
<EVENT VALUE="NOREPAGE">
<EVENT VALUE="MESEND">
